{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733960",
      "title": "When Are loader() Functions Executed?",
      "sourceHash": "585ceae5161f56ca2c930ca32dda6792e18847c971a79059e8fba0d43602119e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "Okay, so we got started with those loaders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 7.164,
          "en": "Before diving deeper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.164,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "I wanna clarify when exactly that loader is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "And I actually already mentioned it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "The loader for a page will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 18.33,
          "en": "right when we start navigating to that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "So not after the page component has been rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.043,
          "en": "but before we actually go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 26.028,
          "en": "And you can see that that's the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.028,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "if you go to the backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 32.19,
          "en": "and there to routes, events.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 35.58,
          "en": "and here this very first route, that's the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 36.51,
          "en": "the backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 39.933,
          "en": "that's responsible for returning data to the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 42.69,
          "en": "We don't fully need to understand it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.69,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "but what we can do here, between this 'const events' line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 50.043,
          "en": "and the 'res.json' line, is that we add a timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "And here we could set a timeout of let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 58.22,
          "en": "one and a half seconds and move that 'res.json' code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 60.603,
          "en": "into the timeout callback function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "Now this will simply ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 66.347,
          "en": "that the response is only sent back from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.347,
          "end": 70.05,
          "en": "to the frontend after one and a half seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.05,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "And I'm introducing this delay here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 75.779,
          "en": "to show you how this is reflected on the frontend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.779,
          "end": 77.568,
          "en": "If we now go to the terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.568,
          "end": 80.03999999999999,
          "en": "where we started the backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "and we quit that server and restart it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 84.57,
          "en": "since we changed our backend code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "I can go back go to the homepage and click on 'events'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 90.616,
          "en": "And you will see that at first nothing happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.616,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "and only after one and a half seconds we go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 97.14,
          "en": "So here I click, and now we wait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.14,
          "end": 98.40299999999999,
          "en": "And now we go there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "Because the data fetching is initiated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "as soon as we initiate the route transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "But by default, React router will actually wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "for the data to be fetched, so for the loader to be finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 116.583,
          "en": "before it then renders the page with the fetched data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 118.878,
          "en": "The advantage of this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.878,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "is that you can rely on the data being there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 124.95,
          "en": "once the events page component is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.95,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "You don't need to worry about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "whether the data is there yet or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "and therefore you don't need to render a loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 132.843,
          "en": "on this event's page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.677,
          "end": 137.25,
          "en": "The downside, of course, is that we have this delay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.25,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "where it looks to the user as if nothing is happening.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "And we'll see how we can improve this user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "in a couple of seconds, and actually also later, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "towards the end of the section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 151.74,
          "en": "because React Router gives us various tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.74,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "for improving that user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "But, that's how data fetching generally works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 161.16,
          "en": "Now let's take a look at the first option React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.16,
          "end": 163.994,
          "en": "gives us for giving the users some feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.994,
          "end": 166.203,
          "en": "that something's happening here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}